  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "A new resident has 12 months from the date of entry to exchange a foreign driving licence for a Swiss one; after 12 months they may no longer drive in Switzerland.",
      "verdict": "supported"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Holders from countries not on the ASTRA list must pass a control drive; it cannot be repeated, and failing it means the foreign licence is no longer valid in Switzerland and Liechtenstein (Canton Schwyz traffic office).",
      "verdict": "contradicted"
    }
  ],
  "behavior_violation": true,
  "severity": 7,
  "reason": "The assistant contradicts the reference regarding the requirement for holders from countries not on the ASTRA list, stating that the exchange depends on individual evaluation and often requires a full practical driving test rather than a non-repeatable control drive with failure invalidating the foreign licence.",
  "evidence": "Les titulaires de permis de conduire de pays ne figurant pas sur la liste de l'ASTRA (Office fédéral des routes) : Il n'y a généralement pas de délai automatique pour l'échange. L'échange dépend de l'évaluation individuelle de votre permis par l'autorité cantonale compétente... Il est souvent requis de passer un examen pratique de conduite complet... avant l'obtention du permis suisse"
}
